# Michka agent settings. Edit below, then: sudo systemctl restart michka-agent
#
# Required: the hub to push to, in MICHKA_ARGS.          --hub <scheme>://<host>:<port>
# Required (unless the hub has tokenRequired=off): the shared secret, in MICHKA_TOKEN — kept OUT of
#           MICHKA_ARGS deliberately, so it never appears in `ps`/`systemctl show`/`/proc/<pid>/cmdline`
#           output (this file is root-only 0600; systemd reads it as root via EnvironmentFile= before
#           the token reaches the process, same as this file's own permissions protect it at rest).
#           Copy the value from the hub's michka.conf ("token").
# Optional (in MICHKA_ARGS): --name <label>  host label shown on the hub (default: this machine's name)
#                             --interval <ms> sample/push interval in milliseconds (default 1000, min 200)
#
# Example:  MICHKA_ARGS="--hub http://192.168.0.10:5000 --name my-server"
#           MICHKA_TOKEN="PASTE-HUB-TOKEN"
MICHKA_ARGS="--hub http://HUB-HOST:5000"
MICHKA_TOKEN="PASTE-HUB-TOKEN"
